stands out because it activates a minor piece, unblocks the queen, and keeps options open for kingside castling after appropriate preparation. It does not block the queen like N: b8-d7 would, and unlike moving the knight, it allows us to keep the knight on f6 (already well-placed) and consider repositioning it later if needed. Additionally, the bishop on d7 can support a future ...Rg8 or ...Ne5 ideas.\n\nAnswer: B: c8-d7'}
