ximizing piece activity and potential initiative — is N: f6-g4.\n\nReason:  \nN: f6-g4 increases pressure on the center and threatens indirect attacks on White’s vulnerable back rank, particularly f2. It develops a minor piece to a strong, active square, avoids passivity, and creates tactical possibilities. This move improves piece coordination and keeps initiative, which is crucial in dynamic positions.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-g4"}
